{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779070690996,"sessionID":"ses_1c71fcd35ffelsR8Et8AZicKn5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_n5w5xVQZAlyQVYHFgHkya8Qm","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"CL_000105[678]|CD14|lacks expression|lacks plasma membrane part|PR_000001396|RO_0002161|term_tracker_item","path":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","include":"cl-edit.owl"},"output":"Found 102 matches (showing first 100)\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl:\n  Line 1107: Declaration(Class(obo:CL_0001056))\n\n  Line 1108: Declaration(Class(obo:CL_0001057))\n\n  Line 1109: Declaration(Class(obo:CL_0001058))\n\n  Line 3550: Declaration(AnnotationProperty(obo:RO_0002161))\n\n  Line 4098: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hematopoietic_stem_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000037 \"A stem cell from which all cells of the lymphoid and myeloid lineages develop, including blood cells and cells of the immune system. Hematopoietic stem cells lack cell markers of effector cells (lin-negative). Lin-negative is defined by lacking one or more of the following cell surface markers: CD2, CD3 epsilon, CD4, CD5 ,CD8 alpha chain, CD11b, CD14, CD19, CD20, CD56, ly6G, ter119.\")\n\n  Line 4163: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000041 \"Eosinophils are CD125-positive (IL-5R), GM-CSFR-positive, IL-3R-positive, VLA4-positive. They can also express MHC Class I & II, CD4, CD9, CD11a, CD11b, CD11c, CD13, CD15, CD16, CD17, CD18, CD24, CD25,CD28, CD29, CD32, CD33, CD35, CD37, CD39, CD43, CD44, CD45, CD45RB, CD45RO, CD46, CD47, CD48, CD49d, CD49f, CD50, CD52, CD53, CD54, CD55, CD58, CD59, CD62L, CD63, CD65, CD66, CD69, CD71, CD76, CD80, CD81, CD82, CD86, CD87, CD88, CD89, CD92, CD95, CD97, CD98, CD99, CD100, CD101, CD116, CD117, CD119, CD120, CD123, CD124, CD125, CD131, CD137, CD139, CD148, CD149, CD151, CD153, CD156, CD162, CD161, CD162, CD165, CD174, CD182, CD183, CD191, CD192, CD193, CD196, CD213, IL9R, ad integrin, beta-7 integrin, FceRI, IL13Ra1, TGFbR, PAFR, LTB4R, C3aR, CystLT1R, CystLT2R, fMLPR, CRTH2 (PGD2 receptor), histamine 4R, IDO, KYN, PAR-2, Siglec-8, Siglec-10, LIR1, LIR2, LIR3, LIR7, TLR7, TLR8, and VLA-4. Eosinophils can also secrete CXCL1, eotaxin-1, GM-CSF, IL-2, IL-3, IL-4, IL-5, IL-6, IL-8, IL-10, IL-12, IL-13, IL-16, IL-18, IFN-gamma, LTC4, MIP-1alpha, NGF, PAF, RANTES, substance P, TGF-alpha, TGF-beta, TNF-alpha, and VIP.\")\n\n  Line 4665: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000091 \"Markers: Mouse: F4/80+, CD11b-low, CD68+, sialoadhesin+, CD163/SRCR+; role or process: immune, antigen-presentation, clearance of senescent erythrocytes, iron metabolism. Kupffer cells are also reportedly C3aR-positive, CD14-low, CD54-positive, CD88-positive, and CD284-positive. They are also capable of producing IL-1, IL-6, TNF-alpha, nitric oxide, PGD2, PGE2, PGF2alpha, and TXA2.\")\n\n  Line 5062: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23616747\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000129 \"Unlike macroglial cells, microglial cells  arise from hematopoietic stem cells in the yolk sac during early embryogenesis that populate the central nervous system. They derive from embryonic mesoderm and are not from neuroectoderm where glioblast develops from. Markers: Mouse: CD11b+, F4/80+, CD68+. They represent ~12% of the cells in the CNS, but they are not uniformly distributed within the CNS. A normal adult mouse brain has approximately 3.5x10e6 microglia. Microglia are also reportedly CD3-negative, CD4-positive, CD8-negative, CD11b-positive, CD11c-high, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD45-low, CD56-negative, CD163-negative, CD200R-positive, CD281-positive, CD282-positive, CD283-positive, CD284-positive, CD285-positive, CD286-positive, CD287-positive, CD288-positive, CD289-positive, Gr1-negative, nestin-positive, and PU.1-positive.\")\n\n  Line 5117: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000134 \"Many but not all mesenchymal cells derive from the mesoderm. MSCs are reportedly CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD5-negative, CD8-negative, CD11a-negative, CD11b-negative, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD29-positive, CD31-negative, CD34-negative, CD38-negative, CD40-negative, CD44-positive, CD45-negative, CD49-positive, CD54-positive, CD66b-negative, CD79a-negative, CD80-negative, CD102-positive, CD106-positive, CD117-positive, CD121a-positive, CD121b-positive, CD123-positive, CD124-positive, CD133-negative, CD146-positive, CD166-positive, CD271-positive, B220-negative, Gr1-negative, MHCI-positive, MHCII-negative, SSEA4-negative, sca1-positive, Ter119-negative, and glycophorin A-negative. Cultured MSCs are capable of producing stem cell factor, IL7, IL8, IL11, TGF-beta, cofilin, galectin-1, laminin-receptor 1, cyclophilin A, and MMP-2.\")\n\n  Line 5128: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000135 \"Cultured human fibrocytes are MHCI-positive, MHCII-positive, CD1a-negative, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD8-negative, CD10-negative, CD11b-positive, CD13-positive, CD14-negative, CD16-negative, CD18-positive, CD19-negative, CD25-negative, CD29-positive, CD32-positive, CD33-negative, CD34-positive, CD38-negative, CD40-positive, CD44-negative, CD45RO-positive, CD49a-positive, CD49b-positive, CD49c-negative, CD49d-negative, CD49e-positive, CD49f-negative, CD56-negative, CD58-positive, CD61-positive, CD64-positive, CD70-negative, CD71-positive, CD80-positive, CD83-negative, CD86-positive, CD103-negative, CD105-positive, CD181-positive, CD182-negative, CD183-positive, CD184-positive, CD185-negative, CD186-negative, CD191-positive, CD192-negative, CD193-positive, CD194-positive, CD195-positive, CD196-negative, CD197-positive, CD199-positive, desmin-negative, F4/80-positive, Gr1-positive, LSP-1-positive, MHCI-positive, MHCII-positive, alpha-SMA-negative, TCRab-negative, TCRgd-negative, and vimentin-positive. Fibrocytes are also capable of secreting angiogenin, bFGF, CCL2, CCL3, CCL4, CCL8, CXCL1, type I collagen, type III collagen, CTGF, fibronectin, GM-CSF, IL-1a, IL-6, IL-8, IL-10, M-CSF, MMP-9, PDGF-A, TGF-alpha, TGF-beta1, TNF-alpha, and VEGF-A.\")\n\n  Line 5466: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000169 \"Pancreatic beta cells are also reportedly CD284-positive. Upon activation, they upregulate their CD14 expression.\")\n\n  Line 6018: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000233 \"Platelets are reportedly CCR1-positive, CCR2-negative, CCR3-positive, CCR4-positive, CCR5-negative, CCR6-negative, CCR7-negative, CCR8-negative, CCR9-negative, CCR10-negative, CD16-positive, CD23-positive, CD32-positive, CD40-positive, CD41-positive CD42-positive, CD61-positive, CD62P-positive, CD64-positive, CD89-positive, CD102-positive, CD147-positive (activated platelets), CD154-positive (activated platelets), CD162-positive, CD209, CD282-positive, CD284-positive, CD289-positive, CD181-negative, CD182-negative, CD183-negative, CD184-positive, CLEC2-positive, GPVI-positive, JAMC-positive, PAR1-positive, PAR2-negative, PAR3-positive, PAR4-positive, TSP1-positive, and TXA2R-positive. Platelets can reportedly produce CCL2, CCL3, CCL5, CCL7, CCL17, CD40L, CXCL1, CXCL4, CXCL4L1, CXCL5, CXCL7, CXCL8, CXCL12, EGF, factor V, factor VII, factor XI, factor XIII, bFGF, histamine, IGF-1, IL-1beta, PAI-1, PDGF, plasminogen, protein S, serotonin, TGF-beta, TFPI, VEGF, and vWF.\")\n\n  Line 6817: AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000341 obo:NCBITaxon_33511)\n\n  Line 7045: AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000371 obo:NCBITaxon_33208)\n\n  Line 7139: AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000385 obo:NCBITaxon_33511)\n\n  Line 7174: AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000390 obo:NCBITaxon_33511)\n\n  Line 7654: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000453 \"Originally described in the dendritic cell ontology (DC_CL:0000021 )(PMID:19243617). These cells are also CD1a-high, CD14-negative, CD207-positive (langerin), CD324-positive (E-cadherin), and DCIR-positive. They reside in the epidermis.\")\n\n  Line 8172: AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000519 obo:NCBITaxon_33511)\n\n  Line 8178: AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0000520 obo:NCBITaxon_2759)\n\n  Line 8488: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000553 \"The earliest cytologically identifiable precursor in the thrombocytic series. This cell is capable of endomitosis and lacks expression of hematopoieitic lineage markers (lin-negative).\")\n\n  Line 8503: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000553 \"Lineage negative is described here as CD2-negative, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD5-negative, CD8a-negative, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD20-negative, CD56-negative, Ly6g-negative, and Ter119-negative.\")\n\n  Line 8644: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000566 \"These cells are reportedly CD31-positive, CD34-positive, CD144-positive, CD309-positive, and TAL1-positive.\")\n\n  Line 8736: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000576 \"Morphology: Mononuclear cell, diameter, 14 to 20 _M, N/C ratio 2:1-1:1. Nucleus may appear in variety of shapes: round, kidney, lobulated, or convoluted. Fine azurophilic granules present; markers: CD11b (shared with other myeloid cells), human: CD14, mouse: F4/80-mid,GR1-low; location: Blood, but can be recruited into tissues; role or process: immune & tissue remodelling; lineage: hematopoietic, myeloid.\")\n\n  Line 9056: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000611 \"These cells are CD34-positive, CD45RA-negative, CD71-negative, and lineage-negative (CD2, CD3 epsilon, CD4, CD5, CD8a, CD14, CD19, CD20, integrin alpha-M, NCAM-1, SCA-1, Ly6G, Ly76).\")\n\n  Line 9079: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000613 \"BaP are also CD13-low and integrin beta-7-low. They are lin-negative (CD2, CD3e, CD4, CD5, CD8, CD11b, CD14, CD19, CD20, ly6g, ly76, and NCAM-1). They also lack expression of mast cell protease 1 (MCP-1) and microphthalmia-associated transcription factor (mitf).\")\n\n  Line 9610: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000669 \"Pericytes are CD10-positive, CD13-positive, CD31-negative, CD45-negative, CD106-positive, CD117-negative, CD140-positive, CD144-negative, CD146-positive, CD271-positive, CD325-positive, NG2-positive, RGS5-positive, SMA-positive, and desmin-positive. A subpopulation is CD248-positive. They are also capable of producing angiopoietin 1, CXCL12, TGF-beta, and VEGF-A.\")\n\n  Line 10431: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000767 \"Matures in the bone marrow and account for <1% of leukocytes in the peripheral blood, spleen, and bone marrow. Basophils are described as being CD11a-positive, CD11b-positive, CD13-positive, CD15-positive, CD18-positive, CD21-positive, CD25-positive, CD29-positive, CD35-positive, CD40-positive, CD40L-positive, CD44-positive, CD45R-negative, CD46-positive, CD49a-positive, CD49b-positive, CD49d-positive, CD55-positive, CD59-positive, CD62L-positive, CD63-positive, CD69-positive, CD90-negative, CD116-positive, CD117-negative, CD124-positive, CD125-positive, CD131-positive, CD161-positive, CD184-positive, CD191-positive, CD192-positive, CD197-positive, CD200R3-positive, CD218-positive, CD282-positive, CD284-positive, CD289-positive, CD290-positive, CD294-positive, natural killer cell receptor 2B4-positive, smad1-positive, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD7-negative, CD8-negative, CD14-negative, CD15-negative, CD16-negative, CD19-negative, CD20-negative, CD34-negative, CD36-negative, CD45R-negative, CD56-negative, CD57-negative, CD235a-negative, and GR1-negative. Transcription factors- GATA1-positive, PU.1-positive.\")\n\n  Line 10477: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000771 \"Eosinophils are also CD14-negative, CD32-positive, CD44-positive, CD48-positive, CD69-positive, CD192-negative, MBP1-positive, MBP2-positive, TLR2-negative, TLR4-negative, and lineage-negative (B220, CD2, CD14, CD19, CD56, CD71, CD117, CD123, CD235a (glycophorin A), and TER119). The cytokines IL-3, IL-5, and GM-CSF are involved in their development and differentiation. Usually considered CD16-negative, CD16 is observed on eosinophilic metamyelocyte.\")\n\n  Line 10600: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000782 \"These cells are CD1a-negative, CD1b-positive, CD11a-positive, CD11c-positive, CD13-positive, CD14-negative, CD20-negative, CD21-negative, CD33-positive, CD40-negative, CD50-positive, CD54-positive, CD58-positive, CD68-negative, CD80-negative, CD83-negative, CD85j-positive, CD86-positive, CD89-negative, CD95-positive, CD120a-negative, CD120b-positive, CD123-negative, CD178-negative, CD206-negative, CD207-negative, CD209-negative, and TNF-alpha-negative. Upon TLR stimulation, they are capable of producing high levels of TNF-alpha, IL-6, CXCL8 (IL-8).\")\n\n  Line 11255: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000831 \"MCP are CD16-positive, CD32-positive, CD34-positive, CD45-positive, integrin beta-7-positive, and lin-negative (CD2, CD3e, CD4, CD5, CD8a, CD14, CD19, CD20, CD27, integrin alpha-M, ly6c, ly6g, NCAM-1, and ter119). These cells also express the transcription factors GATA-1, GATA-2, and MITF, but not C/EBPa.\")\n\n  Line 11725: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16507898\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37232741\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000881 \"A border associated macrophage that is adjacent to a small blood vessel of a brain. A perivascular macrophage expresses the markers CD14, CD16 and CD163. In homeostatic conditions, this central nervous system macrophage has a non-motile cell body with extending and retracting projections through the blood vessel wall.\")\n\n  Line 12414: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17100874\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000937 \"Cell committed to natural killer cell lineage that has the phenotype CD122-positive, CD34-positive, and CD117-positive. This cell type lacks expression of natural killer receptor proteins.\")\n\n  Line 12596: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18432934\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20839338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9785673\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000956 \"A pre-B-I cell is a precursor B cell that expresses CD34 and surrogate immunoglobulin light chain (VpreB , Lambda 5 (mouse)/14.1 (human)) on the cell surface, and TdT, Rag1,and Rag2 intracellularly. Cell type carries a D-JH DNA rearrangement, and lacks expression of immunglobulin heavy chain protein.\")\n\n  Line 13335: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17922016\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19286519\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001029 \"Common dendritic precursor is a hematopoietic progenitor cell that is CD117-low, CD135-positive, CD115-positive and lacks plasma membrane parts for hematopoietic lineage markers.\")\n\n  Line 13339: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001029 \"Surface markers are for mouse cells. Originally described in the dendritic cell ontology (DC_CL:0000041) CDP are reportedly CD2-negative, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD5-negative, CD8a-negative, CD11c-positive, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD20-negative, CD56-negative, B220-negative, Ly6g-negative, MHCII-positive, and Ter119-negative. (PMID:19243617).\")\n\n  Line 13567: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001053 \"A memory B cell that lacks expression of surface IgD.\")\n\n  Line 13574: # Class: obo:CL_0001054 (CD14-positive monocyte)\n\n  Line 13576: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001054 \"A monocyte that expresses CD14 and is negative for the lineage markers CD3, CD19, and CD20.\")\n\n  Line 13578: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001054 \"This cell type is compatible with the HIPC Lyoplate markers for 'monocyte'. Note that while CD14 is considered a reliable marker for human monocytes, it is only expressed on approximately 85% of mouse monocytes.\")\n\n  Line 13579: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001054 \"CD14-positive monocyte\")\n\n  Line 13583: # Class: obo:CL_0001055 (CD14-positive, CD16-low monocyte)\n\n  Line 13585: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20628149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001055 \"An intermediate monocyte that is CD14-positive and with low amounts of CD16.\")\n\n  Line 13588: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001055 \"CD14-positive, CD16-low monocyte\")\n\n  Line 13592: # Class: obo:CL_0001056 (dendritic cell, human)\n\n  Line 13594: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001056 \"A dendritic cell with the phenotype HLA-DRA-positive.\")\n\n  Line 13595: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0001056 \"dendritic cell\")\n\n  Line 13596: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001056 \"This cell type is compatible with the HIPC Lyoplate markers for 'dendritic cell'. The inclusion of HLA-DRA in the definition restricts this definition to human dendritic cells.\")\n\n  Line 13597: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001056 \"dendritic cell, human\")\n\n  Line 13598: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0001056 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000451 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000002015) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606)))\n\n  Line 13599: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0001056 obo:CL_0000451)\n\n  Line 13601: # Class: obo:CL_0001057 (myeloid dendritic cell, human)\n\n  Line 13603: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001057 \"A myeloid dendritic cell with the phenotype HLA-DRA-positive.\")\n\n  Line 13604: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0001057 \"myeloid dendritic cell\")\n\n  Line 13605: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001057 \"This cell type is compatible with the HIPC Lyoplate markers for 'myeloid dendritic cell'. The inclusion of HLA-DRA in the definition restricts this definition to human myeloid dendritic cells.\")\n\n  Line 13606: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001057 \"myeloid dendritic cell, human\")\n\n  Line 13607: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0001057 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000782 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000002015) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606)))\n\n  Line 13608: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0001057 obo:CL_0000782)\n\n  Line 13610: # Class: obo:CL_0001058 (plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human)\n\n  Line 13612: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001058 \"A plasmacytoid dendritic cell with the phenotype HLA-DRA-positive, CD123-positive, and CD11c-negative.\")\n\n  Line 13613: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0001058 \"plasmacytoid dendritic cell\")\n\n  Line 13614: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001058 \"This cell type is compatible with the HIPC Lyoplate markers for 'plasmacytoid dendritic cell'. The inclusion of HLA-DRA in the definition restricts this definition to human plasmacytoid dendritic cells.\")\n\n  Line 13615: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001058 \"plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human\")\n\n  Line 13616: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0001058 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000784 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000001013) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001865) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000002015) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606)))\n\n  Line 13617: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0001058 obo:CL_0000784)\n\n  Line 13705: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001066 \"A progenitor cell committed to the erythroid lineage. This cell is ter119-positive but lacks expression of other hematopoietic lineage markers (lin-negative).\")\n\n  Line 14569: # Class: obo:CL_0002057 (CD14-positive, CD16-negative classical monocyte)\n\n  Line 14571: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15615263\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1706877\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19689341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002057 \"A classical monocyte that is CD14-positive, CD16-negative, CD64-positive, CD163-positive.\")\n\n  Line 14577: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002057 \"CD14-positive, CD16-negative classical monocyte\")\n\n  Line 15193: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002107 \"An IgD-negative CD38-positive IgG memory B cell is a CD38-positive IgG-positive that has class switched and lacks expression of IgD on the cell surface with the phenotype IgD-negative, CD38-positive, and IgG-positive.\")\n\n  Line 15519: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002139 \"These cells are reportedly CD31-positive, CD34-positive, CD144-positive, TAL1-positive.\")\n\n  Line 15875: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:source <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/589>) obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0002174 obo:NCBITaxon_50557)\n\n  Line 17737: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19652886\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002342 \"A circulating endothelial cell of the phenotype CD146-positive, CD105-positive, CD45-negative. This cell type is indicative of recent vascular damage.\")\n\n  Line 18248: # Class: obo:CL_0002394 (CD141-positive myeloid dendritic cell)\n\n  Line 18250: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2882828\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2882837\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17332250\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20628149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002394 \"A myeloid dendritic cell found in the blood, lymph nodes, tonsil, bone marrow, and spleen that is CD141-positive (BDCA-3), XCR1-positive, and Clec9A-positive. This cell-type can cross-present antigen to CD8-positive T cells and can produce inteferon-beta.\")\n\n  Line 18254: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002394 \"CD141-positive myeloid dendritic cell\")\n\n  Line 18268: # Class: obo:CL_0002396 (CD14-low, CD16-positive monocyte)\n\n  Line 18270: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20870168\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002396 \"A patrolling monocyte that is CD14-low and CD16-positive.\")\n\n  Line 18275: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002396 \"CD14-low, CD16-positive monocyte\")\n\n  Line 18280: # Class: obo:CL_0002397 (CD14-positive, CD16-positive monocyte)\n\n  Line 18282: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20628149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21937707\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002397 \"A CD14-positive monocyte that is also CD16-positive and CCR2-negative.\")\n\n  Line 18286: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002397 \"This cell type is compatible with the HIPC Lyoplate markers for 'CD16+ monocyte'. Markers are associated with human cells. Note that this cell type encompasses both human intermediate monocytes (CD14+, CD16-low), and human non-classical monocytes (CD14-low, CD16+).\")\n\n  Line 18287: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002397 \"CD14-positive, CD16-positive monocyte\")\n\n  Line 19045: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002471 \"Gr1-low non-classical monocyte that lacks expression of a MHC-II complex.\")\n\n  Line 19216: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MP:0002407\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002489 \"A thymocyte that lacks expression of CD4 and CD8.\")\n\n  Line 19574: # Class: obo:CL_0002526 (CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell)\n\n  Line 19576: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19236899\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20309010\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002526 \"A dermal dendritic cell that is CD1a-negative and CD14-positive.\")\n\n  Line 19577: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002526 \"CD14+ dermal DC\")\n\n  Line 19579: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002526 \"CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell\")\n\n  Line 19583: # Class: obo:CL_0002527 (immature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell)\n\n  Line 19585: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002527 \"An immature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell is CD80-low, CD86-low, and MHCII-low.\")\n\n  Line 19586: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002527 \"immature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell\")\n\n  Line 19590: # Class: obo:CL_0002528 (mature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell)\n\n  Line 19592: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002528 \"A mature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell is CD80-high, CD86-high, MHCII-high and is CD83-positive.\")\n\n  Line 19593: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002528 \"mature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell\")\n\n  Line 19600: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20309010\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002529 \"A dermal dendritic cell that is CD1a-positive and CD14-negative.\")\n\n  Line 20542: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002629 \"Mature microglia are reportedly CCR2-positive, CD4-positive, CD9-positive, CD11a-positive, CD11b-positive, CD11c-positive, CD13-positive, CD16-positive, CDw17-positive, CD18-positive, CD21-positive, CD26-negative, CD32-positive, CD35-positive, CD36-positive, CD40-positive, CD44-positive, CD45-positive, CD53-positive, CD54-positive, CD56-negative, CD58-positive, CD63-positive, CD64-positive, CD66-positive, CD80-positive, CD86-positive, CD87-positive, CD92-positive, CD106-positive, CD107a-positive, CD147-positive, CD155-positive, CD162-positive, CD163-positive, CD171-negative, CD200R-positive, CXCR3-positive, CX3CR1-positive, fibronectin-positive, GD3-positive, GLUT1-positive, GLUT3-negative, GLUT5-positive, MHCI-positive, MHCII-positive, P2X4-positive, RFD7-negative, RGS5-negative, alpha-SMA-negative, vimentin-positive, and vwf-negative. Mature microglia are capable of producing BDNF, CCL3, CCL5, CCL7, CCL8, CCL9, CCL19, CCL20,CD40L, CSF, CXCL1, CXCL2, CXCL4, CXCL5, CXCL8, CXCL9, CXCL10, glutamate, IL-1beta, IL-1ra, IL-3, IL-6, IL-10, IL-12, LT, MMP-2, MMP-9, NGF, nitric oxide, ROS, TGF-beta, TNF-alpha.\")\n\n  Line 22926: AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002161 obo:CL_0008015 obo:NCBITaxon_7742)\n\n  Line 25162: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0017009 obo:CL_0001056)\n\n  Line 25534: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22726837\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25843402\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25926446\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27194328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37336974\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020010 \"A GABAergic projection neuron located in the external segment of the globus pallidus (GPe) and defined by its exclusive projection to the dorsal striatum rather than to the subthalamic nucleus or basal ganglia output nuclei. In rodents and primates, it is characterized molecularly by expression of FOXP2, MEIS2, and NPAS1, and lacks expression of canonical pallidal markers NKX2-1 and LHX6 (Dodson et al., 2015; Abdi et al., 2015; Courtney et al., 2023). This neuron is GABAergic (GAD1/2⁺, SLC32A1/VGAT⁺) and typically PV⁻, forming the transcriptionally and developmentally LGE-derived subclass of GPe neurons (Dodson et al., 2015; Mallet et al., 2012).\")\n\n  Line 25658: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36338137\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020021 \"A mesenchymal progenitor cell located in fibrocartilaginous tissues, along the fibrochondrocytic differentiation pathway that co-expresses both fibrochondrocyte markers (COL1A1, COL3A1) and mesenchymal stem cell markers (MCAM/CD146, MYLK) in humans. This cell serves as a progenitor for mature fibrochondrocytes and other meniscal cell types, with differentiation regulated by TGF-β signaling, focal adhesion, and extracellular matrix-receptor interaction pathways.\")\n\n\n(Results truncated: showing 100 of 102 matches (2 hidden). Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":102,"truncated":true},"title":"CL_000105[678]|CD14|lacks expression|lacks plasma membrane part|PR_000001396|RO_0002161|term_tracker_item","time":{"start":1779070690954,"end":1779070690993}},"id":"prt_e38e06682001A9wVFQlkMcCxo9","sessionID":"ses_1c71fcd35ffelsR8Et8AZicKn5","messageID":"msg_e38e04f77001bcgYx7zHGZ9ZZn"}}
