{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779070831276,"sessionID":"ses_1c71fcd35ffelsR8Et8AZicKn5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_H1B0mVhaQwec6PTlMBfaLttU","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I added CD14-negative phenotype information to `CL_0001057` (myeloid dendritic cell, human) and `CL_0001058` (plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human), while leaving the broader `CL_0001056` (dendritic cell, human) unchanged in line with the discussion about CD14-positive human DC subsets.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+## Summary\n+\n+This PR addresses issue #3163 by adding CD14-negative phenotype information to the two requested human dendritic cell terms:\n+\n+- `CL_0001057` myeloid dendritic cell, human\n+- `CL_0001058` plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human\n+\n+The broader `CL_0001056` dendritic cell, human term was intentionally not changed, because the issue discussion notes that some human dendritic cells, including tissue-specific subsets, may express CD14.\n+\n+## Changes Made\n+\n+- Updated textual definitions for `CL_0001057` and `CL_0001058` to include CD14-negative phenotype wording.\n+- Preserved the existing `PMID:22343568` definition reference.\n+- Added the requested OMIP references as additional definition xrefs:\n+  - `PMID:34260151`\n+  - `PMID:36470845`\n+  - `PMID:37254600`\n+  - `PMID:38343094`\n+  - `PMID:40095400`\n+- Added logical `lacks_plasma_membrane_part some CD14` axioms using the existing CL relation `CL_4030046` and existing CD14 identifier `PR_000001012`.\n+\n+## Rationale\n+\n+The requested terms already model human-specific dendritic cell phenotypes using HLA-DRA and taxon constraints. Adding `CL_4030046 some PR_000001012` follows existing CL modeling for marker-negative phenotypes and makes the CD14-negative gating characteristic computable without applying it to the broader human dendritic cell class.\n+\n+## Checklist\n+\n+- [x] Read imported issue title, body, and comments from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- [x] Checked existing axioms for `CL_0001056`, `CL_0001057`, and `CL_0001058`.\n+- [x] Confirmed existing modeling relation for marker absence: `CL_4030046` (`lacks_plasma_membrane_part`).\n+- [x] Confirmed existing CD14 identifier usage: `PR_000001012`.\n+- [x] Updated only `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` for committed ontology changes.\n+- [x] Left `CL_0001056` unchanged based on the issue discussion.\n+- [x] Ran `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit.ofn` successfully.\n+- [x] Ran `robot reason -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-reasoned.owl` successfully.\n+\n+Signed-off-by: GitHub Copilot\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I added CD14-negative phenotype information to `CL_0001057` (myeloid dendritic cell, human) and `CL_0001058` (plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human), while leaving the broader `CL_0001056` (dendritic cell, human) unchanged in line with the discussion about CD14-positive human DC subsets.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@\n+## Summary\n+\n+This PR addresses issue #3163 by adding CD14-negative phenotype information to the two requested human dendritic cell terms:\n+\n+- `CL_0001057` myeloid dendritic cell, human\n+- `CL_0001058` plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human\n+\n+The broader `CL_0001056` dendritic cell, human term was intentionally not changed, because the issue discussion notes that some human dendritic cells, including tissue-specific subsets, may express CD14.\n+\n+## Changes Made\n+\n+- Updated textual definitions for `CL_0001057` and `CL_0001058` to include CD14-negative phenotype wording.\n+- Preserved the existing `PMID:22343568` definition reference.\n+- Added the requested OMIP references as additional definition xrefs:\n+  - `PMID:34260151`\n+  - `PMID:36470845`\n+  - `PMID:37254600`\n+  - `PMID:38343094`\n+  - `PMID:40095400`\n+- Added logical `lacks_plasma_membrane_part some CD14` axioms using the existing CL relation `CL_4030046` and existing CD14 identifier `PR_000001012`.\n+\n+## Rationale\n+\n+The requested terms already model human-specific dendritic cell phenotypes using HLA-DRA and taxon constraints. Adding `CL_4030046 some PR_000001012` follows existing CL modeling for marker-negative phenotypes and makes the CD14-negative gating characteristic computable without applying it to the broader human dendritic cell class.\n+\n+## Checklist\n+\n+- [x] Read imported issue title, body, and comments from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- [x] Checked existing axioms for `CL_0001056`, `CL_0001057`, and `CL_0001058`.\n+- [x] Confirmed existing modeling relation for marker absence: `CL_4030046` (`lacks_plasma_membrane_part`).\n+- [x] Confirmed existing CD14 identifier usage: `PR_000001012`.\n+- [x] Updated only `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` for committed ontology changes.\n+- [x] Left `CL_0001056` unchanged based on the issue discussion.\n+- [x] Ran `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit.ofn` successfully.\n+- [x] Ran `robot reason -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-reasoned.owl` successfully.\n+\n+Signed-off-by: GitHub Copilot\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","rel